cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its result artifacts, please cite the paper."
license: MIT
title: "Choosing Defect Detectors by False-Alarm Budget: A Controlled Study of Supervised Contrastive Learning for Radiographic Weld Inspection"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zham1lya/DefectCon"
abstract: >-
  Code and result artifacts for DefectCon, a supervised-contrastive detector for
  tiny defects in industrial radiographic images. The reported numbers can be
  recomputed from the released per-image scores with tests/test_paper_numbers.py.
authors:
  - family-names: Saparova
    given-names: Zhamilya
    affiliation: "Department of Industrial Engineering, University of Ulsan"
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Sudong
    affiliation: "Department of Industrial Engineering, University of Ulsan"
keywords:
  - defect detection
  - supervised contrastive learning
  - radiographic inspection
  - weld inspection
  - anomaly detection
  - reproducibility
